program            = 001_int_args
area               = 07_variadics
description        = Integer variadic arguments retrieved in order: int, unsigned int and long long, folded and volatile-runtime variants
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Header exception: this program includes <stdarg.h>. That is the one sanctioned header
exception for area 07, because variadic functions cannot be written at all without
va_list, va_start, va_arg, va_end and va_copy. stdarg.h is in bcc's own bundled
freestanding set (docs/technical-specifications.md line 208) and is also a freestanding
header supplied by the reference compiler, so it compiles identically under both oracles
and the program remains a single-file reproducer. No other header is included; in
particular stdio.h is not included, because bcc ships none. printf is hand-declared.
Variadic discipline: va_start names count, the last named parameter, in every helper.
Each helper retrieves exactly count arguments, and each call site supplies exactly that
many, so no va_list is ever read past its arguments. Each va_start has exactly one
matching va_end in the same function. No va_copy and no va_list forwarding appear here.
Retrieval types match the supplied argument types exactly: va_arg(ap, int) for int
arguments, va_arg(ap, unsigned int) for unsigned int arguments, va_arg(ap, long long)
for long long arguments. int, unsigned int and long long are not subject to the default
argument promotions, so no promotion adjustment is needed.
Arithmetic: no signed overflow is possible. int arguments are accumulated into long long,
unsigned int arguments into unsigned long long (both widening, same signedness, so no
cast and no -Wconversion diagnostic), and the long long totals stay far inside the 64-bit
range. There is no shift, no division, no aliasing violation, no read of uninitialized
storage, no object modified twice between sequence points, and no dependence on padding
or on the addresses of unrelated objects.
Evaluation order: main stores each helper's return value in a named temporary before
printing it, so no call has more than one side-effecting argument. In the runtime
variants each volatile object is read by a single simple assignment into a plain local
before the call, so the arguments in the call expression are pure reads of plain locals
and the unspecified argument-evaluation order is unobservable.
Warning gate: this program compiles clean under the default gate in full, that is
-Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror, with no
diagnostic on any of the four targets, so it claims no deviation and the optional
gate-deviation key ub_audit_flags is deliberately absent rather than restated: a
record naming the entire default gate would declare a deviation that deviates in
nothing, and a deviation is expressed only as a removal from that gate, with its
reason recorded here.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
Width normalization: the type long and the type unsigned long are never used, because
sizeof(long) and sizeof(void *) are 4 on i686 and 8 on x86-64, AArch64 and RISC-V 64
(docs/technical-specifications.md lines 457 to 462). Only int, unsigned int, long long
and unsigned long long appear, and the printf conversions are limited to %s, %d, %u,
%lld and %llu. No address, no pointer value and no sizeof result is printed. No plain
char value is printed, so the measured plain-char signedness difference (signed on
x86-64 and i686, unsigned on AArch64 and RISC-V 64) cannot affect the output. All
unsigned literals carry the u suffix and all long long literals carry the LL suffix, so
their types are target-independent.
Cross-backend comparability: integer variadic argument passing was measured to produce
byte-identical results on all four targets at all three optimization levels, so no
target is restricted and all three oracles are enabled.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
